From 3aa2440575ae0c486f577caef7dc9a0638fddd08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Mark bit-level and std-backed leaf helpers trusted for now

Bodies using shifts, masks, popcount, wrapping/checked arithmetic,
div_ceil, TryInto, u64::MAX-scale constants, std iterator searches, or
ReprFlags constants cannot be analyzed; they get placeholder
requires(true)/ensures(true) specs to be replaced by real ones later.
This covers Hash64::wrapping_add, the Size, Align, TargetDataLayout,
Niche and Integer helpers, the ReprFlags/ReprOptions flag queries, the
DenseBitSet / BitMatrix / BitIter family, and univariant /
univariant_biased / scalar_pair, which stay a trusted library per the
verification plan. No body is changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
